{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q9BX95","uniProtkbId":"SGPP1_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Sphingosine-1-phosphate phosphatase 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"SPPase1"},{"value":"Spp1"},{"value":"hSPP1"},{"value":"hSPPase1"}],"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12815058"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16782891"}],"value":"3.1.3.-"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Sphingosine-1-phosphatase 1"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"16782891"}],"value":"Sphingosine-1-phosphate phosphohydrolase 1"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"16782891"}],"value":"SPP-1"}]}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:17720"}],"value":"SGPP1"},"synonyms":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"16782891"}],"value":"SPP1"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9JI99"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11756451"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12815058"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16782891"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18583713"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20798685"}],"value":"Specifically dephosphorylates sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P), dihydro-S1P, and phyto-S1P. Does not act on ceramide 1-phosphate, lysophosphatidic acid or phosphatidic acid (PubMed:16782891). Sphingosine-1-phosphate phosphatase activity is needed for efficient recycling of sphingosine into the sphingolipid synthesis pathway (PubMed:11756451, PubMed:12815058, PubMed:16782891). Regulates the intracellular levels of the bioactive sphingolipid metabolite S1P that regulates diverse biological processes acting both as an extracellular receptor ligand or as an intracellular second messenger (PubMed:11756451, PubMed:12815058, PubMed:16782891). Involved in efficient ceramide synthesis from exogenous sphingoid bases. Converts S1P to sphingosine, which is readily metabolized to ceramide via ceramide synthase. In concert with sphingosine kinase 2 (SphK2), recycles sphingosine into ceramide through a phosphorylation/dephosphorylation cycle (By similarity). Regulates endoplasmic-to-Golgi trafficking of ceramides, resulting in the regulation of ceramide levels in the endoplasmic reticulum, preferentially long-chain ceramide species, and influences the anterograde membrane transport of both ceramide and proteins from the endoplasmic reticulum to the Golgi apparatus (PubMed:16782891). The modulation of intracellular ceramide levels in turn regulates apoptosis (By similarity). Via S1P levels, modulates resting tone, intracellular Ca(2+) and myogenic vasoconstriction in resistance arteries (PubMed:18583713). Also involved in unfolded protein response (UPR) and ER stress-induced autophagy via regulation of intracellular S1P levels (PubMed:18583713, PubMed:20798685). Involved in the regulation of epidermal homeostasis and keratinocyte differentiation (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000006DEB2"}},
{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P10451","uniProtkbId":"OSTP_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"1974876"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2726470"}],"value":"Osteopontin"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Bone sialoprotein 1"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Nephropontin"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Secreted phosphoprotein 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"SPP-1"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"1729712"}],"value":"Urinary stone protein"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"1729712"}],"value":"Uropontin"}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"SPP1"},"synonyms":[{"value":"BNSP"},{"value":"OPN"}],"orfNames":[{"value":"PSEC0156"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P31096"}],"value":"Major non-collagenous bone protein that binds tightly to hydroxyapatite. Appears to form an integral part of the mineralized matrix. Probably important to cell-matrix interaction"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P10923"}],"value":"Acts as a cytokine involved in enhancing production of interferon-gamma and interleukin-12 and reducing production of interleukin-10 and is essential in the pathway that leads to type I immunity"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI0000000E0B"}},
{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P16070","uniProtkbId":"CD44_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"CD44 antigen"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"CDw44"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Epican"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Extracellular matrix receptor III"},"shortNames":[{"value":"ECMR-III"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"GP90 lymphocyte homing/adhesion receptor"}},{"fullName":{"value":"HUTCH-I"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Heparan sulfate proteoglycan"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Hermes antigen"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Hyaluronate receptor"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Phagocytic glycoprotein 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"PGP-1"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Phagocytic glycoprotein I"},"shortNames":[{"value":"PGP-I"}]}],"cdAntigenNames":[{"value":"CD44"}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"CD44"},"synonyms":[{"value":"LHR"},{"value":"MDU2"},{"value":"MDU3"},{"value":"MIC4"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15123640"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16541107"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18757307"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19703720"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22726066"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23589287"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"37006235"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7528188"}],"value":"Cell-surface receptor that plays a role in cell-cell interactions, cell adhesion and migration, helping them to sense and respond to changes in the tissue microenvironment (PubMed:16541107, PubMed:19703720, PubMed:22726066). Participates thereby in a wide variety of cellular functions including the activation, recirculation and homing of T-lymphocytes, hematopoiesis, inflammation and response to bacterial infection (PubMed:7528188). Engages, through its ectodomain, extracellular matrix components such as hyaluronan/HA, collagen, growth factors, cytokines or proteases and serves as a platform for signal transduction by assembling, via its cytoplasmic domain, protein complexes containing receptor kinases and membrane proteases (PubMed:18757307, PubMed:23589287). Such effectors include PKN2, the RhoGTPases RAC1 and RHOA, Rho-kinases and phospholipase C that coordinate signaling pathways promoting calcium mobilization and actin-mediated cytoskeleton reorganization essential for cell migration and adhesion (PubMed:15123640). Upon interaction with LGALS9 ligand, activates downstream signaling components including LCK, ERK and MAPK to promotes NK cell activation (PubMed:37006235)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"40544280"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Promotes foot-and-mouth disease virus internalization via macropinocytosis"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000013D3FE"}},
